    "summary": "Kalaga fragment, illustrating scenes from the Ramayana. Hanuman is seen five times in episodes in Lanka. Scenes include, from left, a figure shooting an arrow, Hanuman flying through the air carrying a rock (possibly carrying the Mountain of Herbs or Building the Bridge to Lanka), Hanuman talking to a sage (with two hares below), who, in the next scene is revealed as a demon, Hanuman with a demon figure in a tank, and Ravana receiving demon courtiers. The appliqued figures are made of coloured flannel and cotton (some glued), with sequins, silver thread, and artificial metallic thread fabric, all stitched on to a black velvet ground.",
